00:19:43.280 --> 00:20:02.540
<v Joshuah Bearman>By the time it was done, the stakeout had lasted eight hours. And despite all the red flags, Pete still believed it all. Remember, these people had appeared in all kinds of news stories already. They'd been on the Today show. Pete presumed they'd been vetted and fact-checked. And there was going to be a whole reality show about the Moms. It was just about to start filming.
<v Joshuah Bearman>到结束时，监视行动已经持续了八个小时。尽管有所有的危险信号，皮特仍然相信这一切。记住，这些人之前已经出现在各种新闻报道中了。她们上过《今日秀》。皮特推测她们已经经过审查和事实核实。而且会有一整个关于妈妈们的真人秀。拍摄马上就要开始了。

00:20:02.540 --> 00:20:13.420
<v Joshuah Bearman>So Pete went home that day thinking, this is awesome. The desperate client. The tender-yet-tough PI Moms. The sweat-licking. And he started writing up his story. Until--
<v Joshuah Bearman>所以皮特那天回家时心想，这太棒了。绝望的客户。温柔又强硬的“妈妈侦探”。舔汗水。他开始写他的故事。直到——

00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:43.890
<v Pete Crooks>So this first email was sent on Monday, January 3, 2011 at 12:21 PM, with the subject line "Peter Crooks, Important, PI Moms." "Hi. I am writing this as a courtesy to you. It would be a mistake to publish the article on the PI Moms and Chris Butler that you came and did a story on a few months ago. Chris totally played you. The case that you sat in on was totally scripted."
<v Pete Crooks>所以第一封电子邮件是在2011年1月3日，星期一，下午12:21发送的，主题是“皮特·克鲁克斯，重要，妈妈侦探”。“嗨。我写这封信是出于礼貌。发表你几个月前去做的关于‘妈妈侦探’和克里斯·巴特勒的文章是个错误。克里斯完全在戏弄你。你参与的那个案件完全是脚本化的。”

00:20:43.890 --> 00:20:47.030
<v Joshuah Bearman>So this is an anonymous message.
<v Joshuah Bearman>所以这是一条匿名信息。

00:20:47.030 --> 00:21:06.210
<v Pete Crooks>Well, it was a message from somebody named Rutherford with an email account that you could easily make-- you know, it seemed to me that this person's name was not Rutherford. It was somebody who had made up a new, Yahoo or Gmail account to contact me anonymously.
